 <longdesc><para unique="1046156">This instruction either (a) copies one word element from an XMM register to a general-purpose register or memory location or (b) copies one word element from a general-purpose register or memory location to an XMM register. When writing a general-purpose register, the lower 16-bits of the register will contain the word value. The upper bits of the general-purpose register are written with zeros.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1046158">VMOVW dest, src (two operand load)</title>
   <programlisting>DEST.word[0] := SRC.word[0]
DEST[MAXVL:16] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1046162">VMOVW dest, src (two operand store)</title>
   <programlisting>DEST.word[0] := SRC.word[0]
// upper bits of GPR DEST are zeroed</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <para unique="1046166">VMOVW short _mm_cvtsi128_si16 (__m128i a);</para>
  <para unique="1046167">VMOVW __m128i _mm_cvtsi16_si128 (short a);</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046169">None</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046174" format="xIndent1">EVEX-encoded instructions, see <link unique="1046172" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#32485: 06_Table: Table 2-57. Type E9NF Class Exception Conditions" xrefstyle="Table All - no page with period">Table&#160;2&#8209;59, &#8220;Type E9NF Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
